# Oracle samples, round r11 (2026-11-02).
# Format: BRANCH | ID | WHAT IT PROBES -> OUTPUT THAT CONFIRMS IT | SCRIPT
# SCRIPT is one batch file; "\n" separates its lines (written with CRLF). Run as a .bat file.
A | C1 | caret before the CALL label colon -> SUB, then BACK if the caret is removed | @echo off\ncall ^:sub\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
A | C2 | caret inside a CALL label -> SUB, then BACK if the caret is removed | @echo off\ncall :s^ub\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
A | C3 | colon after a CALL label -> SUB, then BACK if : ends the label | @echo off\ncall :sub:x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
B | P1 | continuation line starting with ^| -> what prints | @echo off\necho a ^\n^| findstr a
B | P1b | continuation line starting with ^| into find -> what prints | @echo off\necho abc ^\n^| find "b"
B | P2 | continuation line starting with ^& -> R11X=1 if the joined line splits at & | @echo off\nset R11X=0\necho x ^\n^& set R11X=1\nset R11X
B | K1 | child cmd split at ^^^& after a block with escaped ) -> CHILDSPLIT if it splits | @cmd /c (echo IN ^) ^^^& echo CHILDSPLIT
B | K1b | same with set in child and parent echo -> env_changes and [..] show which side ran | @cmd /c (dir ^>nul ^) ^^^& set R11K=1 ^& echo [%R11K%]
A | L1 | GOTO with three colons -> END alone if extra colons are stripped | @echo off\ngoto :::end\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
A | L2 | quoted GOTO label -> END alone if quotes are accepted | @echo off\ngoto ":end"\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
